  "architecturalPlan": {
    "scaleRationale": "This is a deliberately expansive single-storey waterfront estate: approximately 390 m² of enclosed principal accommodation plus a substantial sheltered ocean terrace, arrival court, pool surround and detached open-air lounge. The low, spread composition suits a completely flat Saint Lucia oceanfront property, keeps every major room directly connected to exterior living, and invests the $25 million ambition in generous spans, deep shade, crafted material contrast and a complete arrival-to-water sequence rather than unnecessary storeys.",
    "arrivalAndCirculation": "Arrival is assumed from the landward south side. A limestone approach court leads to a recessed bronze front door beneath a dedicated canopy. The entrance opens directly into the tall central living salon, with bedroom wings branching west and east. The oceanward axis continues through broad glazed openings to a shaded terrace, pool court and a detached open elliptical ocean lounge pavilion.",
    "volumeHierarchy": "The double-height central salon is the unmistakable primary volume. Two lower, broad bedroom/service wings extend laterally from it as quiet subordinate bars. The entrance canopy, ocean terrace canopy and pavilion read as lighter outdoor structures, creating a clear progression from protected landward arrival to open seaward living.",
    "relationshipsAndViews": "The central salon is oriented toward the assumed ocean outlook to the north, with three separate framed glazed bays rather than an indiscriminate glass curtain. Its terrace is immediately beyond, shaded by a deep flat canopy and structured by timber posts. The lateral wings retain comparatively solid, private external edges while their inner walls connect back to the central living volume. The pool court and pavilion extend the same central axis without claiming a surveyed shoreline.",
    "roofFacadeAndMaterials": "A family of thin, deep flat roofs unifies the low wings, taller salon, entry threshold and terrace canopy. Limestone ground planes and coping establish a durable base palette; ivory walls provide calm tropical mass; bronze doors and slatted screens add depth; timber posts and pavilion furniture soften the ocean-facing outdoor rooms. Material selections express coastal character only and are not corrosion, waterproofing, hurricane, drainage or thermal-performance certifications.",
    "intendedSpaces": [
      "Covered landward arrival court and recessed entrance threshold",
      "Double-height central living and entertaining salon",
      "West private bedroom-suite wing",
      "East private bedroom-suite and flexible service wing",
      "Large covered ocean-view dining and lounge terrace",
      "Rectangular pool court with explicit perimeter coping and basin floor",
      "Detached open elliptical ocean lounge pavilion"
    ],
    "designDecisions": [
      {
        "disposition": "constructed",
        "knowledgeId": "estate-composition",
        "decision": "Organized the estate as arrival, central salon, shaded ocean terrace, pool court and a subordinate open pavilion; private wings remain secondary to the main residence.",
        "elementIds": [
          "arrival-court",
          "entry-door",
          "salon-floor",
          "salon-roof",
          "ocean-terrace",
          "pool-water",
          "ocean-pavilion"
        ],
        "limitation": "Individual bedrooms and service rooms are spatially represented by wings, not fully partitioned interior fit-outs."
      },
      {
        "disposition": "constructed",
        "knowledgeId": "tropical-envelope",
        "decision": "Used deep canopies, shaded view glazing and selective bronze screens to support a tropical indoor-outdoor lifestyle.",
        "elementIds": [
          "terrace-canopy",
          "terrace-post-west",
          "terrace-post-east",
          "salon-view-left",
          "salon-view-center",
